    "runtime": "Docker (redis:8.10.3, valkey/valkey:9.1.3, dragonflydb/dragonfly:v2.1.0, kividb/kividb:v1.2.0) with Docker's default seccomp profile plus the io_uring syscalls and memlock unlimited; memtier_benchmark 2.5.1; RESP2, no TLS"
  },
  "protocol": {
    "warmups": 2,
    "runs": 10,
    "processModel": "Container per engine, network_mode host, seccomp: Docker's default profile plus io_uring_setup, io_uring_enter and io_uring_register, memlock unlimited: Dragonfly 64 proactor threads and KiviDB 62 worker threads (its default, cores − 2), both on io_uring, on 64 physical cores; Redis and Valkey single-threaded I/O (default io-threads 1); 16 GiB maxmemory for all four",
    "cacheState": "Preloaded keyspace, 100% hit ratio on GET workloads; working sets sized below 50% of maxmemory; eviction flags set for parity of intent, never triggered",
    "output": "memtier_benchmark 2.5.1: ops/s, p50/p99/p99.9 latency, client CPU per 10 s pass; memory via INFO MEMORY: baseline-corrected used_memory and used_memory_rss (process RSS) deltas for the first and second million keys, the absolute RSS after the first million, and random-byte values on a second fresh engine",
    "clientSizing": "memtier: 50 threads × 4 clients = 200 connections"
  },
  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "small-value-throughput",
      "title": "Small value throughput",
      "deck": "SET/GET mix (1:10 ratio) with 100-byte values, pipeline depth 1. RESP2, no TLS.",
      "unit": "ms",
      "lowerIsBetter": true,
      "verdict": {
        "winnerId": "dragonfly",
        "headline": "Dragonfly 1.42M ops/s at the lowest p99 (0.41 ms); KiviDB 1.51M (0.45 ms), the most ops/s on every pass; Valkey 177K (2.10 ms); Redis 176K (2.11 ms)",
        "summary": "SET/GET mix (1:10) at pipeline depth 1 with 100-byte values, 200 connections. The section ranks on p99, and Dragonfly's mean was 41 µs lower than KiviDB's, right at the noise threshold: twice the standard error of that difference is also 41 µs, with KiviDB's p99 swinging from 0.311 to 0.527 ms across passes and Dragonfly's from 0.383 to 0.439. KiviDB's throughput lead is well outside its noise: its slowest pass, 1.49M ops/s, beat Dragonfly's fastest, 1.43M. Valkey and Redis were within 1% of each other at about an eighth of that throughput, and client CPU stayed under 35% on every pass."
      },
